WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.852
A language model predicts token sequences conditioned on its input.

00:00:04.002 --> 00:00:08.367
Tokens are model-specific pieces of text, not necessarily words.

00:00:08.517 --> 00:00:12.470
A context window limits the information that can be considered in one

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.447
request; it is not durable memory.

00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:18.963
More context may increase cost and latency and may distract from relevant

00:00:18.963 --> 00:00:19.327
evidence.

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:24.048
An output token limit bounds generation length, not factual accuracy.

00:00:24.198 --> 00:00:29.800
Temperature influences sampling, but setting it to zero does not guarantee identical

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.068
behavior across providers, model revisions, or hardware.

00:00:33.218 --> 00:00:36.420
A confident sentence is not a calibrated probability.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:40.471
Treat generated statements as claims that may require verification.

00:00:40.621 --> 00:00:44.997
Separate the model’s language capability from access to current business data, which

00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:47.184
must come from retrieval or tools.

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:51.422
The question Where is A100 contains almost no order information.

00:00:51.572 --> 00:00:55.046
Without the lookup tool, the model cannot know today’s status.

00:00:55.196 --> 00:00:58.529
The lab sends a finite history and limits prediction length.

00:00:58.679 --> 00:01:02.477
If a model server returns an error, the adapter raises a dependency

00:01:02.477 --> 00:01:05.642
failure instead of displaying the error body as an answer.

00:01:05.792 --> 00:01:09.744
Measure prompt length before and after ten retrieved documents are added.

00:01:09.894 --> 00:01:13.732
Estimate cost for 10,000 requests using a price sheet you verify on

00:01:13.732 --> 00:01:15.011
the day of measurement.

00:01:15.161 --> 00:01:17.909
Record both average and worst-case token usage.

00:01:18.059 --> 00:01:23.108
Use the actual model tokenizer or provider usage counters, not a fixed

00:01:23.108 --> 00:01:23.949
words-to-tokens rule.

00:01:24.099 --> 00:01:28.824
Multiply separately by input and output rates, add repeated agent calls, and

00:01:28.824 --> 00:01:31.581
state whether caching or batch discounts apply.

00:01:31.731 --> 00:01:33.935
Keep costs as assumptions until measured.

00:01:34.085 --> 00:01:34.756
Question.

00:01:34.906 --> 00:01:37.397
Does a large context window solve memory?

00:01:37.547 --> 00:01:38.124
Answer.

00:01:38.274 --> 00:01:44.907
It supplies a larger temporary input budget; persistence, selection, access control, and

00:01:44.907 --> 00:01:47.118
forgetting remain application responsibilities.

00:01:47.268 --> 00:01:47.939
Question.

00:01:48.089 --> 00:01:51.238
Why can low temperature still produce an incorrect answer?

00:01:51.388 --> 00:01:51.964
Answer.

00:01:52.114 --> 00:01:56.551
Sampling controls variability, not whether the prompt contains enough evidence or whether

00:01:56.551 --> 00:01:58.770
the model learned the fact correctly.
